Package: tufter
Type: Package
Title: Implement Edward Tufte's Principles of Graphical Design
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Charles", "Crabtree",
                  email = "charles.crabtree@monash.edu",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5144-8671"))
Description: A toolkit that turns Edward Tufte's principles of statistical
    graphics into working 'ggplot2' code and into measurements that can be
    applied to an existing figure. The generative side supplies the graphical
    forms Tufte designed or advocated: range frames and quartile frames,
    minimal box plots, dot-dash marginal distributions, bar charts with
    gridlines erased through the bars, sparklines, slopegraphs, small
    multiples, muted palettes, and direct labelling in place of legends. The
    evaluative side supplies the quantities Tufte defined so that a figure can
    be scored rather than admired: the data-ink ratio, estimated empirically by
    rendering the plot with and without its data layers, the lie factor, and
    data density. 'tufte_audit()' runs both sides together and reports which
    principles a plot satisfies. For the underlying principles see Tufte (2001)
    "The Visual Display of Quantitative Information" (ISBN:0961392142), Tufte
    (1990) "Envisioning Information" (ISBN:0961392118), Tufte (1997) "Visual
    Explanations" (ISBN:0961392126), and Tufte (2006) "Beautiful Evidence"
    (ISBN:0961392177).
